Clarchy also ships material that is not covered by that licence and stays under its
owners' terms:

- Cloud provider icons: the AWS Architecture Icons (src/clarchy/data/icons/aws/), the
  Azure architecture icons (src/clarchy/data/icons/azure/) and the Google Cloud icons
  (src/clarchy/data/icons/gcp/), used unchanged under each provider's icon terms. The
  NOTICE.md in each folder gives the source and the terms.
- Open-source project logos (src/clarchy/data/icons/oss/), trademarks of their projects,
  mostly from Simple Icons. Its NOTICE.md lists each logo and its source.
- Fonts (src/clarchy/static/fonts/): Archivo, IBM Plex Sans, IBM Plex Mono, Open Sans and
  Roboto, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, in the LICENSE-*.txt files beside them.
- The Azure service list (src/clarchy/data/directory/azure.yaml) keeps product names and
  summaries from the product directory of Microsoft's Azure documentation
  (https://github.com/MicrosoftDocs/azure-docs, articles/index.yml), licensed under
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
  Clarchy reduces it to a name, category, summary and link per product.
- The Google Cloud service list (src/clarchy/data/directory/gcp.yaml) keeps product names
  and one-line descriptions from https://cloud.google.com/products/.

